                    {
                        "sense_id": "ad19977d-2731-3d18-b340-d2d0b73f1fea",
                        "entry_id": "b95b3740-734d-3458-80a6-25137e01ee2c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A behaviour or manner that is characteristic of a coxcomb; a foppish behaviour."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "usually"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c416cce3-2a21-4ca1-b2ce-8f13b5f0c083",
                                "sense_id": "ad19977d-2731-3d18-b340-d2d0b73f1fea",
                                "text": "He was clean shaved; clean shaving is a favorite coxcombry of the deacon class."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "bfec94e0-f9b0-3197-8f99-e199277a1c7d",
                        "entry_id": "b95b3740-734d-3458-80a6-25137e01ee2c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Behaviour or airs characteristic of a coxcomb; foppishness."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "uncountable",
                            "usually"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ed0f3cfa-59b4-4022-8d50-e19f08603f24",
                                "sense_id": "bfec94e0-f9b0-3197-8f99-e199277a1c7d",
                                "text": "His manner was perhaps the more seductive, / Because he ne'er seem'd anxious to seduce; / Nothing affected, studied, or constructive / Of coxcombry or conquest: no abuse / Of his attractions marr'd the fair perspective, / To indicate a Cupidon broke loose, / And seem to say, \"Resist us if you can\" -- / Which makes a dandy while it spoils a man."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "41281276-6bf6-47b1-9982-ed716efcff53",
                                "sense_id": "bfec94e0-f9b0-3197-8f99-e199277a1c7d",
                                "text": "He paused, grimly regarding it, while a dash of pleased coxcombry seemed to mingle with the otherwise savage satisfaction expressed in his face."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9dd83a39-9a2f-4567-9641-9482fc2409ce",
                                "sense_id": "bfec94e0-f9b0-3197-8f99-e199277a1c7d",
                                "text": "There was a half-sigh floating through his pages for those days of intellectual coxcombry, when ideas come to us affecting the embraces of virgins, and swear to us they are ours alone, and no one else have they ever visited: and we believe them."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "61940e58-fde4-4e88-b4fe-d2d15b68b942",
                                "sense_id": "bfec94e0-f9b0-3197-8f99-e199277a1c7d",
                                "text": "A man emasculated by coxcombry may spend more time upon the arrangement of his clothes than any woman, but even then there is no fetichism in his idea of them--they are still only a covering he uses for a time."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
